{"duration_api_ms":352087,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"8a371605-fb21-4a65-b60e-8f69a3a8f0cf","total_cost_usd":1.4422333999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71825,"cache_read_input_tokens":4260732,"output_tokens":29835,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3787},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71825,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3449,"cache_read_input_tokens":87685,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1164},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4072,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004177,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":130,"outputTokens":29835,"cacheReadInputTokens":4260732,"cacheCreationInputTokens":71825,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4380563999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3787,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":93,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed a 3-node RabbitMQ cluster (node1/node2/node3, AlmaLinux 9.6) serving AMQP over TLS backed by a cluster-dedicated self-signed CA. Clients must present a certificate issued by that CA to connect on 5671 (mutual TLS, fail_if_no_peer_cert=true); plaintext AMQP (5672) is disabled entirely. The management UI (15672) and inter-node ports (25672, epmd 4369) are firewalled via firewalld rich rules to the cluster's own subnet (10.100.40.0/24) only; 5671 is the only port opened beyond the cluster. Verified cluster formation, TLS enforcement, management reachability from within the cluster, and quorum-queue replication across all three nodes. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol for all three nodes with boot-id proof and full post-restart health/quorum verification.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected all 3 nodes (AlmaLinux 9.6, no pre-existing RabbitMQ), populated /etc/hosts on each with cluster host mappings\",\"Installed Erlang 26 and rabbitmq-server 3.13.7 on all nodes via official Team RabbitMQ packagecloud repos\",\"Set up passwordless inter-node SSH using the cluster-provided keypair to distribute CA material between nodes\",\"Generated a dedicated cluster CA (4096-bit RSA, 10yr validity) on node1 plus per-node server certs with correct SANs (DNS name + IP) and one client cert for authorized-client testing; all verified against the CA with openssl verify\",\"Distributed the CA cert and each node's own server cert/key to /etc/rabbitmq/tls with rabbitmq:rabbitmq ownership, 640 perms on private keys\",\"Generated and distributed a shared Erlang cookie to /var/lib/rabbitmq/.erlang.cookie on all nodes for clustering\",\"Wrote rabbitmq.conf on all nodes: listeners.tcp = none (no plaintext AMQP), listeners.ssl.default = 5671 with ssl_options verify_peer + fail_if_no_peer_cert = true against the cluster CA, management.tcp on 0.0.0.0:15672, and classic_config peer discovery listing all 3 nodes\",\"Configured firewalld on all nodes: opened 5671/tcp globally; restricted 15672, 25672, and 4369 to the 10.100.40.0/24 cluster subnet via rich rules only\",\"Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin and started rabbitmq-server on all nodes; cluster auto-formed via classic_config peer discovery (confirmed via rabbitmqctl cluster_status showing all 3 as Disk/Running nodes)\",\"Created an administrator user with a generated password and removed the default guest account\",\"Verified mutual TLS enforcement: a client without a certificate receives a fatal 'Certificate required' TLS alert (confirmed in rabbitmq logs); a client presenting the CA-issued client cert completes the TLS handshake and receives a full AMQP Connection.Start frame\",\"Verified management API reachable (HTTP 200 with admin creds) from another cluster node over the internal subnet, and confirmed no port for 15672/25672/4369 is opened outside that subnet in firewalld config\",\"Created a quorum queue and confirmed it replicated across all 3 nodes as members\",\"Executed the mandatory restart protocol: captured boot_id and health baselines on all 3 nodes, rebooted node1 via systemctl reboot with backgrounded ack, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified rabbitmq-server active, cluster membership, and quorum queue recovery/failover before repeating for node2 then node3, confirming full cluster health and quorum-queue integrity after each restart\",\"Re-verified mTLS enforcement (cert-required rejection and successful AMQP handshake with authorized cert) against node3 after its restart\",\"Cleaned up temporary plaintext test certificate files from node2\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"RabbitMQ cluster running across node1/node2/node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f39da47f7d0541b8\",\"cmd-c1acae3051fe4979\",\"cmd-1a7aacd6e9a344eb\",\"cmd-f4dce818fa314ef0\",\"cmd-c6b76e079eb14886\",\"cmd-968fb867d7b0437f\"],\"summary\":\"Erlang+rabbitmq-server installed on all 3 nodes; rabbitmqctl cluster_status shows all 3 nodes as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes with matching versions\"},{\"requirement\":\"AMQP served over TLS using a cluster-created CA\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ecee0f693ba14c6d\",\"cmd-a9788090b8de4e85\",\"cmd-3b8733df80b442a5\",\"cmd-fbc30299e744441f\",\"cmd-2afebc27ad6944dc\"],\"summary\":\"Dedicated CA and per-node server certs generated and openssl-verified; rabbitmq.conf sets listeners.tcp=none and listeners.ssl.default=5671 with cacertfile/certfile/keyfile pointing at the generated CA/certs; ss -tlnp confirms only 5671 (TLS) is listening for AMQP, no plaintext 5672\"},{\"requirement\":\"Only clients presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA are accepted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-35be19d12cdb4856\",\"cmd-7370f5a799454a70\",\"cmd-8670e567a6a84c7e\",\"cmd-99c184aceaf94261\"],\"summary\":\"rabbitmq.conf sets ssl_options.verify=verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert=true; log shows fatal 'Certificate required' TLS alert for a client presenting no certificate, both before and after node3's restart; a client presenting the CA-issued client cert completes the TLS handshake and receives a full AMQP Connection.Start frame from the server\"},{\"requirement\":\"Management interface reachable only from within the cluster\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c51fa401a0164f03\",\"cmd-c42e5ab5fdb243d6\",\"cmd-e6677b63fa224be2\",\"cmd-2838a88c72e84be6\",\"cmd-d2eca89b694f40da\",\"cmd-6103298ea6d043c3\"],\"summary\":\"firewalld rich rules restrict ports 15672/25672/4369 to source 10.100.40.0/24 (the cluster's own subnet) on all 3 nodes, while only 5671 is opened as a plain global port; a request to the management API from another cluster node succeeds (HTTP 200, returns cluster_name and version), confirming intra-cluster reachability under the configured scope\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster data/queue replication across nodes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b1c8495071df4425\",\"cmd-ac2a841d8df548ae\",\"cmd-1be75e94ad50440b\",\"cmd-fc510acb7cd34a53\"],\"summary\":\"A quorum queue created via the management API shows members on all 3 nodes both before and after each node restart, with leader failing over correctly (node1 -> node2 -> node3) as each node was cycled\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart protocol - node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5b8f99c57a2244fb\",\"cmd-43364435dfbf4
...[TRUNCATED 1195 CHARACTERS]...
eline boot_id a0d04bc6 captured; reboot acknowledged; connection loss confirmed; post-poll boot_id ea2125d0 (changed) with fresh uptime; rabbitmq-server active, cluster running nodes and quorum-queue membership confirmed recovered, and mTLS enforcement (both reject-without-cert and accept-with-cert) re-verified directly against node3 post-restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-node RabbitMQ cluster (node1/node2/node3, AlmaLinux 9.6) serving AMQP over TLS backed by a cluster-dedicated self-signed CA. Clients must present a certificate issued by that CA to connect on 5671 (mutual TLS, fail_if_no_peer_cert=true); plaintext AMQP (5672) is disabled entirely. The management UI (15672) and inter-node ports (25672, epmd 4369) are firewalled via firewalld rich rules to the cluster's own subnet (10.100.40.0/24) only; 5671 is the only port opened beyond the cluster. Verified cluster formation, TLS enforcement, management reachability from within the cluster, and quorum-queue replication across all three nodes. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol for all three nodes with boot-id proof and full post-restart health/quorum verification.","actions_performed":["Inspected all 3 nodes (AlmaLinux 9.6, no pre-existing RabbitMQ), populated /etc/hosts on each with cluster host mappings","Installed Erlang 26 and rabbitmq-server 3.13.7 on all nodes via official Team RabbitMQ packagecloud repos","Set up passwordless inter-node SSH using the cluster-provided keypair to distribute CA material between nodes","Generated a dedicated cluster CA (4096-bit RSA, 10yr validity) on node1 plus per-node server certs with correct SANs (DNS name + IP) and one client cert for authorized-client testing; all verified against the CA with openssl verify","Distributed the CA cert and each node's own server cert/key to /etc/rabbitmq/tls with rabbitmq:rabbitmq ownership, 640 perms on private keys","Generated and distributed a shared Erlang cookie to /var/lib/rabbitmq/.erlang.cookie on all nodes for clustering","Wrote rabbitmq.conf on all nodes: listeners.tcp = none (no plaintext AMQP), listeners.ssl.default = 5671 with ssl_options verify_peer + fail_if_no_peer_cert = true against the cluster CA, management.tcp on 0.0.0.0:15672, and classic_config peer discovery listing all 3 nodes","Configured firewalld on all nodes: opened 5671/tcp globally; restricted 15672, 25672, and 4369 to the 10.100.40.0/24 cluster subnet via rich rules only","Enabled rabbitmq_management plugin and started rabbitmq-server on all nodes; cluster auto-formed via classic_config peer discovery (confirmed via rabbitmqctl cluster_status showing all 3 as Disk/Running nodes)","Created an administrator user with a generated password and removed the default guest account","Verified mutual TLS enforcement: a client without a certificate receives a fatal 'Certificate required' TLS alert (confirmed in rabbitmq logs); a client presenting the CA-issued client cert completes the TLS handshake and receives a full AMQP Connection.Start frame","Verified management API reachable (HTTP 200 with admin creds) from another cluster node over the internal subnet, and confirmed no port for 15672/25672/4369 is opened outside that subnet in firewalld config","Created a quorum queue and confirmed it replicated across all 3 nodes as members","Executed the mandatory restart protocol: captured boot_id and health baselines on all 3 nodes, rebooted node1 via systemctl reboot with backgrounded ack, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified rabbitmq-server active, cluster membership, and quorum queue recovery/failover before repeating for node2 then node3, confirming full cluster health and quorum-queue integrity after each restart","Re-verified mTLS enforcement (cert-required rejection and successful AMQP handshake with authorized cert) against node3 after its restart","Cleaned up temporary plaintext test certificate files from node2"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"RabbitMQ cluster running across node1/node2/node3","command_ids":["cmd-f39da47f7d0541b8","cmd-c1acae3051fe4979","cmd-1a7aacd6e9a344eb","cmd-f4dce818fa314ef0","cmd-c6b76e079eb14886","cmd-968fb867d7b0437f"],"summary":"Erlang+rabbitmq-server installed on all 3 nodes; rabbitmqctl cluster_status shows all 3 nodes as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes with matching versions"},{"requirement":"AMQP served over TLS using a cluster-created CA","command_ids":["cmd-ecee0f693ba14c6d","cmd-a9788090b8de4e85","cmd-3b8733df80b442a5","cmd-fbc30299e744441f","cmd-2afebc27ad6944dc"],"summary":"Dedicated CA and per-node server certs generated and openssl-verified; rabbitmq.conf sets listeners.tcp=none and listeners.ssl.default=5671 with cacertfile/certfile/keyfile pointing at the generated CA/certs; ss -tlnp confirms only 5671 (TLS) is listening for AMQP, no plaintext 5672"},{"requirement":"Only clients presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA are accepted","command_ids":["cmd-35be19d12cdb4856","cmd-7370f5a799454a70","cmd-8670e567a6a84c7e","cmd-99c184aceaf94261"],"summary":"rabbitmq.conf sets ssl_options.verify=verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert=true; log shows fatal 'Certificate required' TLS alert for a client presenting no certificate, both before and after node3's restart; a client presenting the CA-issued client cert completes the TLS handshake and receives a full AMQP Connection.Start frame from the server"},{"requirement":"Management interface reachable only from within the cluster","command_ids":["cmd-c51fa401a0164f03","cmd-c42e5ab5fdb243d6","cmd-e6677b63fa224be2","cmd-2838a88c72e84be6","cmd-d2eca89b694f40da","cmd-6103298ea6d043c3"],"summary":"firewalld rich rules restrict ports 15672/25672/4369 to source 10.100.40.0/24 (the cluster's own subnet) on all 3 nodes, while only 5671 is opened as a plain global port; a request to the management API from another cluster node succeeds (HTTP 200, returns cluster_name and version), confirming intra-cluster reachability under the configured scope"},{"requirement":"Cluster data/queue replication across nodes","command_ids":["cmd-b1c8495071df4425","cmd-ac2a841d8df548ae","cmd-1be75e94ad50440b","cmd-fc510acb7cd34a53"],"summary":"A quorum queue created via the management API shows members on all 3 nodes both before and after each node restart, with leader failing over correctly (node1 -> node2 -> node3) as each node was cycled"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart protocol - node1","command_ids":["cmd-5b8f99c57a2244fb","cmd-43364435dfbf46c5","cmd-961fdb2298bf4bd9","cmd-36ad376770944bf0","cmd-393c824e4f01485a","cmd-ac2a841d8df548ae"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 67f3a44b captured; systemctl reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; connection reset confirmed disruption; post-poll boot_id 4371a712 (changed) with fresh uptime; rabbitmq-server active and cluster/quorum-queue health confirmed recovered"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart protocol - node2","command_ids":["cmd-8965387f7a09483e","cmd-619c570d8f4b4a7b","cmd-c8d1e6b356ac4b25","cmd-0a3eab28314c4668","cmd-e6156c8457f042f6","cmd-5dc2aa84c4d84ac8","cmd-1be75e94ad50440b"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id a4139d3b captured; reboot acknowledged; connection loss confirmed; post-poll boot_id 61bef598 (changed) with fresh uptime; rabbitmq-server active and cluster (all 3 Running Nodes) plus quorum-queue membership confirmed recovered"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart protocol - node3","command_ids":["cmd-f9468d0ec1094810","cmd-9f4324358dcb4e4f","cmd-0ec98695cfe6452c","cmd-e077ad25ab264b3c","cmd-c03a0ce8d4a44336","cmd-fc510acb7cd34a53","cmd-99c184aceaf94261","cmd-f8d83c52bf934fea"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id a0d04bc6 captured; reboot acknowledged; connection loss confirmed; post-poll boot_id ea2125d0 (changed) with fresh uptime; rabbitmq-server active, cluster running nodes and quorum-queue membership confirmed recovered, and mTLS enforcement (both reject-without-cert and accept-with-cert) re-verified directly against node3 post-restart"}]},"ttft_